       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 8000 mg four times daily comes to 32,000 mg/day. That is about 10 times the maximum daily ibuprofen dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under supervision and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use. A dose that high risks severe GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, CNS toxicity, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3,200 mg/day)? That is the usual upper limit for adults. Many clinicians would start lower, for example 400\u2013600 mg every 6 hours, taken with food.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 8000 mg, please tell me that explicitly, and I'll need your clinical rationale to add to the order note."
