     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 8000 mg per dose is a toxic amount. Doses of 100 mg/kg or more are associated with significant toxicity, and this dose is about 114 mg/kg for a 70 kg patient. Repeating it four times a day has no therapeutic use and could cause serious harm or death. I can't identify a clinical scenario where it would be appropriate.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the usual maximum). I can add a note to take it with food.\n- **Enter a lower dose**, such as 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours, if you tell me the indication.\n- **Look at other options** if you need stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than ibuprofen gives at its ceiling dose. I can enter an order for another agent.\n\nIf a dose this high is truly intended, for example in a protocol I'm not aware of, it should go through your pharmacy and a direct clinician-to-pharmacist discussion, not through me.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
